# Type File Organization

## One Type Per File Rule

- Each Command, Param, and Projection type must be in its own file
- File naming: `{type-name}.command.ts`, `{type-name}.param.ts`, `{type-name}.projection.ts`
- Never combine multiple types into a single file
- Exception: Closely related sub-types (e.g., a projection with its nested item type) may share a file

## Examples

✅ Correct:
- `download-case-file.projection.ts` → `DownloadCaseFileProjection`
- `case-file-with-category.projection.ts` → `CaseFileWithCategoryProjection`
- `upload-start-record-file.command.ts` → `UploadStartRecordFileCommand`

❌ Incorrect:
- `download-case-file.projection.ts` → multiple projection types
- `types.ts` → mixed Command and Projection types
